# This repo is text only: scripts, configs, knowledge. Nothing generated, nothing large.
# If you are about to `git add -f` something, ask why it is not reconstructible from
# config/refs.manifest.tsv or a bootstrap script instead.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Nextflow run state
.nextflow
.nextflow.log
.nextflow.log.*
.nextflow.pid
.nextflow/
work/
**/work/
.nf-test/
.nf-test.log
timeline*.html
report*.html
trace*.txt
dag*.html
dag*.svg
dag*.mmd
pipeline_info/
**/pipeline_info/
.nextflow.history

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------- run outputs
# runs/ is the user's own analysis history and never enters git. It says which samples
# they hold and what was done to them — nobody cloning this tool should receive that,
# and once a real patient sample goes through, the accession itself is the disclosure.
# This repo is public.
#
# The agent still reads runs/ locally, at planning time, to notice that a sample has
# been through a pipeline before. That works off the filesystem; git is not involved.
#
# Worked examples of the record format live in docs/examples/ and are committed on
# purpose — they are documentation, not history.
runs/**
!runs/.gitkeep
results/
**/results/
outdir/
**/outdir/

# ------------------------------------------------------- materialised reference store
# /refs is rebuilt by bootstrap/04-refs.sh from the manifest. The manifest is the
# artifact; the bytes are not.
refs/
/refs
.refs/
genomes/
igenomes/
singularity/
.singularity/
containers/
*.sif
*.simg

